.el .ds Aq '
.TH pkgds 1  "pkgds 0.1.1" 
.SH NAME
pkgds \- Real disk usage per package for Arch Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpkgds\fR [\fB\-H \fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-search\fR] [\fB\-\-sort\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-btrfs\fR] [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-dbpath\fR] [\fB\-d \fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-apparent\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-total\fR] [\fB\-\-files\fR] [\fB\-\-tree\fR] [\fB\-\-depth\fR] [\fB\-\-breadth\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-percent\fR] [\fB\-\-with\-deps\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIPOSITIONAL\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Real disk usage per package for Arch Linux
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-H\fR \fI<HUMANSIZE>\fR
Human\-size unit (B, K, Ki, M, Mi, G, Gi, T, Ti, auto, auto\-si; default: raw in format mode, auto in table mode)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
B
.IP \(bu 2
K
.IP \(bu 2
Ki
.IP \(bu 2
M
.IP \(bu 2
Mi
.IP \(bu 2
G
.IP \(bu 2
Gi
.IP \(bu 2
T
.IP \(bu 2
Ti
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
auto\-si
.RE
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-search\fR \fI<SEARCH>\fR
Search packages by regex on name
.TP
\fB\-\-sort\fR \fI<SORT>\fR [default: real]
Sort by field: name (ascending), real (alias size)/apparent/files (descending), ratio (ascending; requires \-\-btrfs)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
name
.IP \(bu 2
real
.IP \(bu 2
size
.IP \(bu 2
apparent
.IP \(bu 2
files
.IP \(bu 2
ratio
.RE
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR
Show only top N packages (0 = unlimited; default 20 in table mode, unlimited in format mode)
.TP
\fB\-\-btrfs\fR
Enable btrfs on\-disk size tokens (%z, %r)
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR [default: /]
Set filesystem root prefix
.TP
\fB\-\-dbpath\fR \fI<DBPATH>\fR
Override pacman local DB path (absolute)
.TP
\fB\-d\fR \fI<DELIM>\fR
Delimiter between packages in format mode (default: newline; used literally, use \-d $\*(Aq\\t\*(Aq for tab)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show warnings for missing files, permission errors
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable color output
.TP
\fB\-\-apparent\-size\fR
Show apparent file size instead of disk blocks (du \-\-apparent\-size)
.TP
\fB\-\-total\fR
Show total row at the bottom of table output
.TP
\fB\-\-files\fR
Show file count column
.TP
\fB\-\-tree\fR
Show a per\-package file/dir tree (default depth 1)
.TP
\fB\-\-depth\fR \fI<DEPTH>\fR
Tree depth in levels (implies \-\-tree; default 1)
.TP
\fB\-\-breadth\fR \fI<BREADTH>\fR
Show at most K children per directory (default 5; requires \-\-tree)
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-percent\fR \fI<MIN_PERCENT>\fR
Prune entries below this percentage of their parent (requires \-\-tree; default 0.1)
.TP
\fB\-\-with\-deps\fR
With targets include freed dependencies; bare ranks all packages by freed space (table only)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIPOSITIONAL\fR]
Format string (printf\-style) or package names

Flags may follow package names (`pkgds bash \-\-btrfs`). A format string that starts with `\-` therefore needs the `\-\-` separator.
.SH EXTRA
FORMAT
  Pass a string containing `%` as the first argument to print one line per
  package with exactly the fields you ask for. Tokens: %n name, %v version,
  %m real disk usage, %a apparent size, %f file count, %p metadata size,
  %z btrfs on\-disk usage (requires \-\-btrfs), %r btrfs ratio, %% literal %.
  `\\t` and `\\n` inside the format string become tab and newline. `\-d`
  is used literally between packages; use shell $\*(Aq\\t\*(Aq for a tab there.

MODES
  Table mode (default) shows the top 20 packages; format mode shows all
  matches unless \-n is given. \-H defaults to auto in table mode and raw
  bytes in format mode. The % share column is omitted when only one
  package matches. A format string takes precedence over \-\-tree. \-\-total
  and \-\-files describe the table and are ignored in the tree view. With
  \-\-btrfs the tree is measured in on\-disk bytes, so a package with no
  on\-disk data is left out and reported on stderr rather than shown.

SELECTION
  \-\-with\-deps expands the named packages (or the \-s/\-\-search matches) to what
  removing them would free: the packages themselves plus every dependency
  that was installed as a dependency and that nothing else needs.
  \-\-sort ratio requires \-\-btrfs. Flags may follow package names
  (`pkgds bash \-\-btrfs`); a format string starting with `\-` needs `\-\-` first.

WITH\-DEPS MODES
  With targets (names or \-s/\-\-search) \-\-with\-deps expands the selection to
  what removing them would free: the targets plus every dependency that was
  installed as a dependency and that nothing else needs. TOTAL is the joint
  freed bytes.
  Bare \-\-with\-deps (no targets, no \-s/\-\-search, no format string) ranks every
  installed package: one row per package, REAL untouched, SAVES is the space
  that removing only that package would free (the package plus the deps that
  would become unneeded). SAVES uses the shown size (REAL, or APPARENT with
  \-\-apparent\-size) summed over that set, so a file claimed by two packages
  counts in each claim and SAVES values overlap; TOTAL and the % column stay
  off in this mode. \-\-sort is ignored (rank is by SAVES, then \-n applies).
  Table only: bare \-\-with\-deps with a format string or \-\-tree is an error.
  \-\-btrfs DISK and RATIO stay per package.

EXIT CODES
  0 success. 1 usage error (bad flag combination, missing paths) or nothing
  matched at all. 2 partial result: some file could not be read, some
  package was malformed, btrfs data was unavailable, or some requested
  package names were unknown. A full scan exits 2 whenever any package owns
  a file this user cannot read, so treat 2 as "numbers are a lower bound",
  not as failure.
.SH VERSION
v0.1.1
